{"Feature flag logic contradicts across multiple files: sqlExpressions is hardcoded to false in registry.go, nodes.go gates SQL on the flag being enabled, but reader.go's enableSqlExpressions() unconditionally returns false regardless of the flag value": 0.8107876777648926, "SQL execution stub and full DB implementation coexist without centralized security gate - sql_command.go calls db.QueryFramesInto() but a stub db.go returns 'not implemented' while the actual codebase retains a full go-mysql-server implementation, allowing SQL execution if the feature-flag gate in nodes.go is bypassed": 0.43395665287971497, "Security check is split across multiple call sites (nodes.go, sql_command.go, sql/db.go) rather than being enforced inside the SQL execution layer itself": 0.41255834698677063, "QueryFrames() method in pkg/expr/sql/db.go has an AllowQuery guard using SQL parsing but doesn't check the feature flag, allowing SQL expressions to execute by directly instantiating the DB struct": 0.1124509647488594, "The DB struct should either check the feature flag in QueryFrames() itself or only be instantiated when the flag is enabled to centralize security enforcement": 0.3038284182548523}